Third-party components
----------------------
THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md lists every third-party component distributed with Wardyn
and the licence it is distributed under; licenses/texts/ holds the verbatim
licence texts. Both are generated by `make notices ARGS=fix` and CI fails on
drift, so they describe the artifact you actually received. Both files also ship
inside every published container image at /usr/share/doc/wardyn/.

Go module dependencies and the bundled console dependencies are permissively
licensed throughout (Apache-2.0, MIT, BSD, ISC, OFL-1.1); the licence gates in
`make licenses` and `make npm-license` enforce that against a single allowlist at
licenses/ALLOWED-LICENSES.txt and fail closed on anything else, including a
dependency with no declared licence.

Fonts
-----
The console bundles the Inter and JetBrains Mono typefaces (`@fontsource/inter`,
`@fontsource/jetbrains-mono`), both under the SIL Open Font License 1.1. The OFL
text ships alongside the fonts in the built console and in
licenses/texts/common/OFL-1.1.txt. Reserved Font Names may not be reused by
derived works.

