GPL components in the published container images
------------------------------------------------
The agent images apt-install `asciinema` (GPL-3.0), which `wardyn-rec` executes as
a subprocess and never compiles into or links with. That disposes of the
derivative-work question but not of the distribution one: publishing an image
conveys those binaries, as it does the GPL and LGPL packages in the Debian and
Alpine base images. deploy/images/THIRD-PARTY-GPL.md carries the corresponding
source offer covering all of them.

Vendor-licensed components
--------------------------
Some agent images bundle a third-party AI coding CLI that is NOT open source and
is governed by that vendor's own terms rather than by any licence in this
repository. Each such image says so in its `org.opencontainers.image.licenses`
label and in deploy/images/THIRD-PARTY-TERMS.md. Read that file before pulling or
redistributing those images.
